1
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone with no money, come to my place!

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,020
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:36,020
Look at the blue sky and the white clouds.

4
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:36,460
Me

5
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:42,900
We'll manage somehow, I'm sure.

6
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without a job, come to my place!

7
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

8
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:18,260
Look, even the crimson sky is burning.
It'll all work out somehow in time.

9
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:27,480
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you get it, follow me quietly.

10
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,480
Ryo-san will grow up big.

11
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,120
Idiot!

12
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:54,600
You should quit the police force right now!

13
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,340
We're acquainted, Chief?

14
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,880
Ryo-chan, what did you do this time?

15
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:03,380
Looks like the Chief caught you
slacking off at the game center.

16
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,120
It was part of our patrol!

17
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,180
See! Heh!

18
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,220
Wow, Ryo-san, that's amazing!

19
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,840
With me, it's a piece of cake!

20
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,000
Is that so! Sounds like a really fun patrol!

21
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:19,520
Next time, take me along too!

22
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,360
Of course, Chief!

23
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,640
It's a lot of fun!

24
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,060
After finally getting forgiven,

25
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,160
if the Chief catches me here,

26
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,280
I'll really get fired this time!

27
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,980
The Chief hates me.

28
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:45,000
He just keeps nagging and yelling,

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,220
never noticing

30
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:48,480
when I'm working hard.

31
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,480
Always, always, always,

32
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:54,760
he only shows up when I take a little
break between shifts to clear my head.

33
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,860
You big idiot!

34
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,080
That's why it's fine.

35
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:07,100
If I'm going to get scolded anyway,
it's better to do what I like.

36
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,020
It's like being a rebellious
kid going through a phase.

37
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,320
So what's the problem?

38
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:15,840
Are you saying you've never slacked
off on the job for even a single second?

39
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:19,220
Th-that's not even one second...

40
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:28,560
No, but look: even if you slack off the same way, you two don't get scolded, but I do.
The Chief really does hate me.

41
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:41,960
Excuse me, how do I get to Kameari Library?
Turn right at the signal up ahead, it's conspicuous, so you'll find it right away.

42
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,060
Haa...

43
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:44,320
Thank you very much.

44
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:50,800
I'm the one who gave the directions, yet being thanked like that...
we're getting along well.

45
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,080
That's always how it is.

46
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,720
That's not true at all.

47
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,140
I was just telling that to Senior Officer too,
you know.

48
00:03:56,140 --> 00:04:00,000
No matter how hard I work honestly,
in the end someone else steals the credit.

49
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:03,480
Looks like there's no use
saying anything right now.

50
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,600
Let's leave him alone for a while.

51
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:12,440
Iri iri, fure iri, hou,
iri iri, fure iri, hou

52
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,900
Professor Emisaki

53
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:19,420
Well, well, if it isn't Gorilla-kun and his friends.
What a coincidence.

54
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:22,460
A coincidence? We're always here, you know.

55
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:24,620
Running into each other here must be fate.

56
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:28,280
If you've got time, would you keep
me company for a bit, Gorilla-kun?

57
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,580
We're on duty right now.
We don't have time for that.

58
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,758
How cold of you.

59
00:04:32,808 --> 00:04:36,220
When I'm in such need of Gorilla-kun's help.

60
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,160
Getting involved with you never ends well.

61
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,020
Well, I suppose it can't be helped.
Just for a little while.

62
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:54,940
Please, have some manju first. Go ahead.

63
00:04:55,960 --> 00:05:01,380
Just ordinary manju?
No way it's that simple.

64
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:06,620
You probably don't believe it,
but this supplement, the Jumbo Manju!

65
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:11,460
Jumbo manju?
Don't tell me eating it makes you bigger?

66
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,180
Ping-pong, table tennis!

67
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:18,580
Any athlete who eats this manju
can have whatever physique they want.

68
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:22,780
It's a revolutionary invention that guarantees victory,
Gorilla-kun.

69
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:26,240
That's practically doping, isn't it?

70
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,420
Well, there's no such people, of course.

71
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:31,860
Getting bigger changes your life,
Gorilla-kun.

72
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:32,980
What?

73
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:38,000
You, who have lived in someone's shadow,
quietly and unnoticed until now,

74
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,620
how enviable.

75
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:42,840
Just by eating this Jumbo Manju,

76
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,920
Bacc-bacc-bacc-bacc!

77
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:48,360
you'll transform into a splendid sportsman.

78
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,760
The girls will be all over you.

79
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,600
They'll be completely smitten.

80
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,580
This great invention, the Jumbo Manju,

81
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,100
is free right now!

82
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:05,180
One piece makes you a little bigger,
you know?

83
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:06,960
Two pieces and you get a bit bigger still.

84
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,560
And if you eat three,

85
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,660
the taste is not bad either.

86
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:15,380
Nothing happens to you at all?

87
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:16,520
What do you mean?

88
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,840
Does your body swell up or something?

89
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:19,660
Not really.

90
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:21,120
Do you get all bulked up?

91
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,160
Not at all.

92
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,880
We should have tested it on a human,
not a gorilla, after all.

93
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,020
I'm human!

94
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,920
Ryo-san's really slow, isn't he?

95
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,160
Ryo-chan

96
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:36,220
Senpai

97
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:40,080
What, you two look like you've shrunk.

98
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,560
No, Senpai just got bigger.

99
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,100
What?

100
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,660
I ate Professor Emisaki's Jumbo Manju.

101
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:49,480
Jumbo Manju.

102
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:53,220
I think it's Professor
Emisaki's new invention.

103
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:56,800
I see. But Ryo-san, you look pretty good.

104
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:59,980
Your legs are long, too.
You look like an NBA player.

105
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,360
Do you think so?

106
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,920
No, you look great.

107
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:07,140
But when your perspective changes like this,

108
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:11,100
all the rudeness you've shown me until now

109
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,500
starts to seem forgivable. How strange.

110
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,420
Isn't it that your heart has
grown as wide and big as your body?

111
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,360
I have a favor to ask.

112
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:27,400
Me?

113
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:27,960
Yes.

114
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:32,280
Getting bigger changes your whole life,
Gorilla-kun.

115
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,360
Here it comes, here it comes!

116
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,880
What do you need?

117
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:42,660
Go ahead.

118
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,420
We're saved!

119
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,340
Consider it done!

120
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:49,920
Decided, then.

121
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,060
No way

122
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,500
And then, would you believe it,

123
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,980
Yacchan

124
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:06,880
Senpai,
you've gotten even bigger than before!

125
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,120
Well, this is a problem.

126
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,080
At this size, you can't live a normal life.

127
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:14,740
You're right. I'll go take a look for a bit.

128
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:16,080
Where are you going?

129
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:23,080
By the way, what about the cake?

130
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,480
Same as always.

131
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:33,300
At this rate, running would be faster.

132
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,240
Move, move, move, move!

133
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:43,640
Ai-ree ai-ree fu-re ai-ree ho!

134
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:46,640
Ai-ree ai-ree fu-re ai-ree ho!

135
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:50,180
Ai-ree ai-ree fu-re ai-ree ho!

136
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:55,620
Well, if it isn't Gorilla-kun.

137
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,980
Looks like the Jumbo Manju worked after all.

138
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,720
How does it feel to be bigger?

139
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,080
This isn't what you promised!
I'm way too big!

140
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,420
Make me go back to a body
about two meters tall.

141
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,280
It doesn't work that conveniently,
Gorilla-kun.

142
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,060
What's that?

143
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:15,600
This is the Super Ultra Hyper Jumbo Manju,
made with concentrated supplements.

144
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,880
Would you like to try some?

145
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,940
No way!
I want a Manju that makes me smaller!

146
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,060
No, it just keeps getting bigger.

147
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:24,040
That's a problem.

148
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:26,480
So I'm supposed to live
at this size forever?

149
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:28,680
No, it won't stay that size forever.

150
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,540
It goes back to normal on its own?

151
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:31,680
That's not it either.

152
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:34,920
Eat one Jumbo Manju and
you get a little bigger.

153
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,140
And if you eat three?

154
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,920
Chomp, chomp, chomp!

155
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,400
And if you eat three?

156
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:46,520
Eat three and you get ridiculously huge!

157
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:47,680
What?

158
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:55,480
Way too big!

159
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:01,720
What?

160
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,460
Aaaaaaah!

161
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:21,920
Yes, it's 8 o'clock in front of the park!
Eeeeeh! A monster is swimming in the sea!

162
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,340
Eeeeeh!

163
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,720
[unintelligible]

164
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,540
I can't believe a creature
like that really exists.

165
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:41,040
But where did it come from?

166
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:44,660
Anyway, get the citizens to a safe place!

167
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:45,440
Hurry!

168
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,940
Could that be...

169
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,400
Senpai.

170
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,440
It's noisy up there, isn't it?

171
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,040
Should we take a quick look?

172
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:21,980
Hey! At least cover up the front!

173
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,000
Buchuu!

174
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:27,740
W-what is going on here!
What do you think you're doing?

175
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:28,816
No, no, this is...

176
00:11:28,866 --> 00:11:32,220
There's a reason for this!
Please help me, buchuu!

177
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,660
Senpai,
how do you like your custom-made uniform?

178
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,078
Mm

179
00:11:38,128 --> 00:11:41,760
It fits perfectly!
Thanks for everything, Nakagawa!

180
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:44,660
I've arranged your daily
necessities for now, but

181
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,740
if you need anything else, just let me know.

182
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,920
Since I'll have to stay here for a while.

183
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:53,640
Well, it's convenient that
the police box is so close.

184
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,440
Still, everyone's so small.

185
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:58,660
You all look like well-made figurines.

186
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,900
Regarding the future, Chief Ohara,

187
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:05,660
Chief, I'll take full
responsibility for supervising him.

188
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:07,160
Please, just as before,

189
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:09,240
let him keep working as Officer Ryotsu.

190
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,580
Please make the arrangements.

191
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:14,300
But with a body that size,
what kind of work can he do?

192
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,660
There must be some job Ryotsu can do.

193
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:18,860
Surely there's something.

194
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:20,040
Ryo-chan.

195
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,440
What is it?

196
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:23,320
It's a freight car derailment.

197
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,020
What?

198
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,680
Ryotsu, it's a job for you!

199
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:30,860
Hey, how's it going over there?

200
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:35,180
The freight car has tipped over

201
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:40,220
Don't worry.

202
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:44,240
Okay, it's dangerous, so everyone step back.

203
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:49,840
It's like a model train
set in the biggest gauge.

204
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:55,820
Dig, dig, dig, dig, dig, dig, dig...

205
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,160
This is a piece of cake.

206
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,140
Well, this is a problem.

207
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,840
So you're the cause of the traffic jam?

208
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:15,720
Ugh, what a pain.
Alright, everyone can go now.

209
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:21,500
Keep moving, keep moving!
What, the Ferris wheel stopped?

210
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:26,300
Come on, get down! What,
the octopus wanted to go up the power line?

211
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,640
The cat can't get down?

212
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:30,720
Ryo-san, help!

213
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,420
Ryo-san, take over here!

214
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,540
Ryo-san, give us a hand!

215
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:34,700
Ryo-san, it's bad!

216
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,880
It was busy again today.

217
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:45,360
Well, time to get some sleep.

218
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:49,320
Chief, what's going on?

219
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:54,160
I thought it might be nice to sleep
outside and look at the stars for a change.

220
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,460
I hear you've been working hard every day.

221
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:04,640
With how conspicuous I am,
I can't even slack off.

222
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:09,620
The station chief is extremely
pleased with your work.

223
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:13,440
If he's pleased, I'd like to see
it shown in something more tangible.

224
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:16,500
I hear he'll treat us to
1,000 servings of yakiniku.

225
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:20,560
I can't suddenly give you alone special treatment,
you know.

226
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,720
There's also the matter
of the other officers.

227
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:28,540
I'm special too,
so surely you can give me special treatment!

228
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,320
Here he comes.

229
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,480
What's all this commotion?

230
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:55,120
The chief is going to give you a
commendation letter for your work.

231
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,360
Good for you.

232
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,960
A commendation letter?

233
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:58,660
That's right.

234
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,060
A commendation letter.

235
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:03,340
Kankichi Ryotsu,
for your recent outstanding work,

236
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:06,380
on behalf of Katsushika Police Station and the citizens of the ward,
we thank you.

237
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:07,020
Thank you.

238
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:10,160
Chief of Katsushika Police Station,
Tomita Gomez.

239
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:15,180
Is a thank-you all I get, Chief?

240
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:19,420
What about the 100 bales of rice and the 1
million yen cash gift from the deputy station?

241
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:20,420
Smooth.

242
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:24,400
After working me to the bone, this is all I get?
Just one piece of paper?

243
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,560
I've been eating emergency signboards every day,
you know.

244
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,240
Ohara-kun.

245
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:33,680
Hey, Ryotsu, don't get carried away.

246
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:37,360
Be grateful you got a
commendation letter at all.

247
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:39,120
I understand perfectly.

248
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:43,040
If you won't give me a reward,
I'm not working anymore.

249
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:47,900
On the contrary,
I might get in the way of citizens' lives.

250
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:52,220
Idiot! Are you even still a police officer?

251
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:55,300
I'd make more money if I
weren't a police officer.

252
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:57,120
Hey, where do you think
you're going, Ryotsu?

253
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,540
Senpai, he's gone.

254
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,340
Ryo-chan.

255
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,300
If it comes to this, I'll survive on my own.

256
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:13,440
The construction was behind schedule,
and I was struggling.

257
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,440
That helps a lot.

258
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,940
Leave it to me.

259
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:19,320
Hey, swing it, swing it, swing it,
swing it, swing it, swing it!

260
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:21,540
Right, secure it quickly!

261
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:27,300
Cut!

262
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:29,300
That's it!

263
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,660
Perfect.

264
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:32,560
Thanks.

265
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:34,240
Gyoro's side too, all right?

266
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,460
OK!

267
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:39,320
I'm beat.

268
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:40,840
Good work.

269
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,160
Good work, senpai.

270
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,020
What's on tomorrow's schedule?

271
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:47,880
Tomorrow we're guests at the
elementary school's sports day,

272
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,760
and the department store by the
station is doing its big cleaning.

273
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:55,200
Then there's the maintenance and the continued filming of Dogira vs.
Mechadogira.

274
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,780
That's a huge amount of work.

275
00:16:57,780 --> 00:17:01,720
Word on the street is he makes
in one day what we earn in a year.

276
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,880
Wow, senpai, you're amazing.

277
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:08,060
I'm doing the work of hundreds of you lot all by myself,
you know.

278
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,960
This is just what's expected.

279
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,060
I'm tired,
so I'm going to bed early tonight.

280
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:13,260
See you tomorrow.

281
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:15,360
Good night, senpai.

282
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:30,180
Well then,
let's have you introduce your friends.

283
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:36,220
We interrupt this program to bring you an emergency press
conference from the Prime Minister's Official Residence.

284
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,540
W-what is it?

285
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:44,520
We have just received an emergency communication
from the President of the United States.

286
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:48,940
In ten hours, a massive meteor
shower will strike the Earth.

287
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:55,200
And the exact impact point of that
meteor shower has now been determined.

288
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:59,060
That location is Kameari,
in Katsushika Ward, Tokyo.

289
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:00,620
Kameari?

290
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:08,920
Can we really count on
Ryotsu to handle this, Ohara?

291
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:12,260
Though it's a meteor shower,
apparently each individual piece is small.

292
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:14,020
We have no other choice.

293
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:16,600
Ryotsu should be able
to do something about it.

294
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:24,560
A meteorite? The price changes depending on its size,
you know.

295
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,560
You idiot! Listen seriously, Ryotsu!

296
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:30,600
The residents of Kameari have
already started evacuating.

297
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,080
This is no time for a side job!

298
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:36,580
Protecting the town of Kameari should come first,
don't you think!

299
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,740
My livelihood is on the line too, Chief.

300
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:43,400
I get incredibly hungry,
so it costs a lot of money.

301
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:46,840
Fine, let's hear your demands.

302
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:50,040
Chief, don't spoil Ryotsu.

303
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,760
Never mind, never mind.

304
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:55,640
Let's see,
1,000 servings of fatty tuna sushi,

305
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,840
1,000 portions of Matsusaka-grade yakiniku,

306
00:18:57,840 --> 00:19:01,400
and for dessert,
1,000 servings of a full Chinese course.

307
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,940
If you feed me all that
every day for a year,

308
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:05,400
I'll take the job.

309
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:08,400
You idiot! Taking advantage of
someone's weakness like that!

310
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,780
Even so, a reduction, is it?!

311
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,660
There are other ways, you know.

312
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:15,300
Karin! Go on, go!

313
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,980
Yes! Ohara-kun!

314
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,622
Ohara-kun,

315
00:19:19,672 --> 00:19:27,320
so what exactly do you intend to do?

316
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:31,580
I'm sorry. Since it's Ryotsu,
I just couldn't help it...

317
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:35,703
A large number of meteorites will
be falling on this area shortly.

318
00:19:35,753 --> 00:19:39,020
It's dangerous,
so please evacuate immediately.

319
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:40,240
I repeat.

320
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:43,840
A large number of meteorites will
be falling on this area shortly.

321
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:46,520
You're all still here?

322
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:47,820
Ryo-chan.

323
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:51,560
Do you remember the commendation
letter we got from the station chief?

324
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:52,960
Commendation letter?

325
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:54,380
You see,

326
00:19:54,380 --> 00:19:58,380
Chief Ohara asked the
station chief to do it for you.

327
00:19:58,920 --> 00:19:59,600
What?

328
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:04,140
We can't raise your salary right away,

329
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:07,560
but we wanted to at least
recognize Ryo-chan's hard work.

330
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:12,340
Chief Ohara wanted Ryo-san to be
able to stay at Katsushika Station.

331
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:17,640
It was Chief Ohara who asked the station chief and
the senior officials at Metropolitan Police HQ, too.

332
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,120
The Chief...

333
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:24,960
Ryo-chan thinks the Chief hates him,
but that's not true at all.

334
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:28,820
Chief Ohara really loves Ryo-chan.

335
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:35,420
They're already here!
You lot, evacuate now, hurry!

336
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:36,700
Got it, Ryo-san!

337
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:40,780
That's it!

338
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:48,360
Bring it on, from wherever you like!

339
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:10,220
Take a look at this.

340
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:13,520
Ryotsu is knocking the
meteors back one after another.

341
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:14,300
Ryotsu!

342
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,840
We've just received new information.

343
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:21,640
The core of this meteor shower
is not high-pressure gas,

344
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,600
but a giant meteorite.

345
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:27,700
This giant meteorite is nearly the
same diameter as the Kameari district,

346
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,100
and the damage from its impact is

347
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:31,980
Tokyo's annihilation.

348
00:21:35,020 --> 00:21:36,600
Tokyo's annihilation.

349
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:39,140
We have to evacuate Ryotsu.

350
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:48,000
Damn, more are coming?

351
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:48,660
Ryotsu!

352
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,680
Ryotsu, that's enough!

353
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:54,040
A giant meteorite is coming!

354
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:55,600
Get out now, hurry!

355
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:57,360
How big is "giant"?

356
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:00,180
They say it's about as
wide as the town of Kameari.

357
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:03,620
What did you say?

358
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:07,460
Hurry and run, Freos! Run at full power!

359
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:11,520
It's the super ultra hyper jumbo manju!

360
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:12,560
That's right!

361
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,840
Over there!

362
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:18,340
Ezagi!

363
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:20,420
It's Gorilla-kun!

364
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:22,260
Do you have any hyper manju?

365
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,760
There's a whole bunch
of hyper ones right here!

366
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:29,860
I'm taking all of them!
You evacuate too, quickly!

367
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:04,980
Alright.

368
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:07,480
There it is.

369
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,160
Keep an eye on the Chief.

370
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:24,100
We did it.

371
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:25,900
The meteorite's trajectory has changed.

372
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:29,580
Earth has been saved
thanks to Ryotsu's heroics.

373
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:32,840
Ryotsu, well done!

374
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:35,840
We did it, Chief!

375
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:42,200
And now, Officer Ryotsu, the man who saved humanity,
is returning to the ground.

376
00:23:42,980 --> 00:23:44,300
Could it be...

377
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:45,840
Isn't this the Chief...

378
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:55,220
No way!

379
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:01,320
You're fired.

380
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:20,520
Like someone is calling out,
a late afternoon after the rain

381
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:24,560
I walked on, looking back

382
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:27,180
led by the hand of the
clattering gacha machines

383
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:30,420
the feeling I had back then

384
00:24:31,420 --> 00:24:34,420
a strange, mysterious feeling

385
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:35,880
That's why

386
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:39,620
the tiles of the arcade street

387
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,380
I tried walking only on the black ones

388
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

389
00:24:54,620 --> 00:25:01,040
the self-important politicians and the
aunties with their trembling eyebrows too

390
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:06,580
Try turning that corner

391
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:11,800
you can meet everyone, everyone

392
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:16,900
Over there, that's Kameari.

393
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:19,900
Well, surely it's Kameari.

394
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:24,940
Everyone, come on over to our town!

395
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

396
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:34,580
Anyway, just call coffee
"bean broth from South America."

397
00:25:34,580 --> 00:25:38,020
If you force it into Japanese, it'll
just be harder to understand, won't it?

398
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:40,600
Even though you're so fixated
on Japanese like that anyway.

399
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:47,300
He's an American! See you next time at
the Yamato Spirit Preservation Society.

400
00:25:48,940 --> 00:25:49,500
Me

401
00:25:53,020 --> 00:25:53,580
Me

402
00:25:58,100 --> 00:25:59,220
to town

403
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:01,140
Aaahhhh

